Validate namespace/queue names as git ref names

Workspace::queue() / Workspace::namespace() return raw selector-file
contents (and the global -q override) without re-validating against git
ref-name rules. Not exploitable today (git2 rejects bad names at write
time, read paths fail safely) but the next code path that bypasses git2
loses the invariant. Tighten at the boundary.

Plan: call namespace::validate_name / queue::validate_name in the
Workspace::namespace() / Workspace::queue() readers (after the selector-
file read or -q override). Same for the remote selector. Add tests
that malformed selector files error cleanly.